      "message": "I don\u0027t think it\u0027s the plan. The priority is to stop adding stuff to ConnectivityServiceTest, so it stops becoming bigger and bigger. But I don\u0027t think it\u0027s realistic to expect that we\u0027re going to remove ConnectivityServiceTest any time soon. We\u0027ll want to group stuff and move stuff opportunistically. This will happen over the next few years. I don\u0027t plan to ever \"complete\" a migration.\n\nIf you\u0027re going to move something opportunistically I don\u0027t think translating into Kotlin is much of an ask – tools do this pretty well already, so you can mostly rely on automatic translation. But also, I don\u0027t think why you think these tools are not java-compatible ? What\u0027s wrong with using CSTest from Java if that\u0027s what you want ?",
